      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 5
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "That would mean that I would see a significant chunk of the users as just default avatars. As someone who likes to see everyone's unique avatar, this would be a major turn-off. I understand the frustration with the ripping, but seeing other people's content is one of the best things about this game. Having this taken away from me would just kill a big part of the game for me. \n\nNot only that, but now people may not accept me as their friend if they aren't sure I wouldn't be ripping their assets. Cool, so this adds a system that actively discourages you from making friends.\n\nHere's a non-destructive solution to the problem: Don't upload.\n\nI know it seems like a silly thing, but the moment you upload to VRChat, someway somehow people will find ways to get access to those files.\n\nIf you want to be in your own avatar but have others see you as a fallback, upload your own avatar as a local test one, then get ingame, pick any of the default avatars of your choice, then select the local test avatar and done, you get to be you while everyone sees you as something else.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
